# Names of pa3ds's own for the parts of each Pokémon in Pokémon-Amie, said by its stylus as it
# comes onto one. The game names none: it keeps a picture of the Pokémon a grey a kind of part,
# the same greys on every Pokémon (spike 287), 17 and 18 electric, 25 and 26 its danger zone, 27
# and 28 its sweet spot. A message a Pokémon's national number and grey: amie-spot-25-17 is
# Pikachu's cheeks. One a form drawn unlike its species adds its form, amie-spot-25-1-27 Pikachu
# Rock Star's, or f for a female, and is said before the species' own. A grey a Pokémon
# has no name for here is said by its kind; the head and the body always are, and the eyes but
# where a model paints them the other way round (Lombre), or one grey on every eye (Claydol).
#
# Each is a body part, two words at most (Orion, 2026-11-05), named from the census of every
# species and form in Amie (spike 287): its screen beside its picture of greys, a part named only
# where the picture shows it, the sweet spots and danger zones a player's petting guide named
# checked against them; then checked again by other agents, each sheet with what pa3ds says
# (2026-11-06). A form whose parts are its species', Burmy's cloaks, East Shellos, takes those
# names. The other languages' are a machine's translation of these (2026-11-08), to be
# corrected.

